[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
## TL;DR  

* **You didn’t miss a step – those APIs simply don’t exist in MapLibre.**  
* `map.setFog()` → **`map.setSky()`** (the “sky” layer replaces Mapbox’s fog/atmosphere).  
* Mapbox’s free-camera helpers (`getFreeCameraOptions`, `setFreeCameraOptions`, `FreeCameraOptions`) → **`map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(...)`** (or the older `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) + `map.jumpTo / map.easeTo / map.flyTo`.  

Everything else (imports, namespace, token removal, style URL, plugins, etc.) should already be in place if you followed the migration guide. Below is a concise “what to change” checklist, plus full code snippets and debugging tips to get your map looking and behaving like it did before.

---

## 1. Verify the “basic” migration steps first  

| ✅ Item | What to check |
|--------|---------------|
| **Package** | `npm uninstall mapbox-gl && npm install maplibre-gl` (or `yarn add maplibre-gl`). |
| **Import / CSS** | ```js\nimport * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';\nimport 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';\n``` |
| **Namespace** | All `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl`. |
| **Access token** | Remove any `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'`. |
| **Style URL** | Use a non-Mapbox style (e.g. `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty` or your own style JSON). |
| **Controls / CSS classes** | `mapboxgl-ctrl` → `maplibregl-ctrl` (if you wrote custom CSS). |
| **Plugins** | Replace Mapbox-only plugins with MapLibre equivalents or open-source forks (see *awesome-maplibre*). |
| **Geocoding / Directions** | Swap Mapbox APIs for Nominatim, OSRM, OpenRouteService, MapTiler, etc. |

If any of those are still pointing at Mapbox, the map will fail to load before you even get to the fog/camera code.

---

## 2. The two “missing” Mapbox v2 APIs

### 2.1 `map.setFog()` → `map.setSky()`

| Mapbox (v2) | MapLibre (v5-v6) |
|-------------|-----------------|
| `map.setFog({ "color": "#fff", "high-color": "#fff", "horizon-blend": 0.3 })` | `map.setSky({ "sky-color": "#fff", "horizon-color": "#fff", "fog-color": "#fff", "horizon-fog-blend": 0.3, "sky-horizon-blend": 0.3 })` |
| Fog is a *style* property (`fog` in the style JSON) | Sky is a *root-level* style object (`sky`) and a *runtime* method (`setSky`). |

#### How to enable the same visual effect

1. **Add a `sky` object to your style JSON** (or let the runtime add it).  
   ```json
   {
     "version": 8,
     "sources": { … },
     "layers": [ … ],
     "sky": {
       "type": "sky",
       "sky-color": "#199EF3",
       "horizon-color": "#ffffff",
       "fog-color": "#c0d8ff",
       "fog-ground-blend": 0.5,
       "horizon-fog-blend": 0.5,
       "sky-horizon-blend": 0.5,
       "atmosphere-blend": 1.0
     }
   }
   ```
2. **Or set it programmatically** (the same way you called `setFog`):
   ```js
   // MapLibre
   map.setSky({
     'sky-color': '#199EF3',
     'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
     'fog-color': '#c0d8ff',
     'fog-ground-blend': 0.5,
     'horizon-fog-blend': 0.5,
     'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
     'atmosphere-blend': 1.0
   });
   ```

> **Note:** `sky` is still marked *experimental* in the spec, but it works in all current releases (v5-v6). If you need a simple “no-sky” map, just omit the `sky` object.

### 2.2 Free-camera helpers → `calculateCameraOptions…` + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`

Mapbox v2 introduced a **FreeCameraOptions** class and the methods:

```js
const opts = map.getFreeCameraOptions();
map.setFreeCameraOptions(opts);
```

MapLibre never implemented those. Instead you compute a `CameraOptions` object yourself and feed it to the normal camera methods.

#### The modern MapLibre way (v5+)

```js
// Desired camera position (lng, lat, altitude in meters)
const lngLat = [ -122.42, 37.78 ];
const altitude = 500;               // meters above ground
const bearing = 45;                 // degrees clockwise from north
const pitch   = 60;                 // degrees
const roll    = 0;                  // degrees (v5.0+)

// Compute the full CameraOptions object
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
  lngLat,
  altitude,
  bearing,
  pitch,
  roll
);

// Apply it – choose the animation you like
map.jumpTo(camOpts);                // instant
// or
map.easeTo({ ...camOpts, duration: 2000 });
// or
map.flyTo({ ...camOpts, curve: 1.5 });
```

#### The older helper (pre-v5, still available in v5)

If you only need a “look-at” from one point to another, you can use the *from-to* helper:

```js
const from = [-122.42, 37.78];
const to   = [-122.45, 37.80];
const altitudeFrom = 200;
const altitudeTo   = 300;

const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromTo(
  from,
  altitudeFrom,
  to,
  altitudeTo,
  { bearing: 30, pitch: 45 }   // optional extra overrides
);

map.easeTo(camOpts);
```

#### Quick migration checklist for camera code

| Mapbox code | MapLibre replacement |
|-------------|----------------------|
| `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` | `map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(...)` (or `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) |
| `map.setFreeCameraOptions(opts)` | `map.jumpTo(opts)` / `map.easeTo(opts)` / `map.flyTo(opts)` |
| `new mapboxgl.FreeCameraOptions()` | **No class** – just build a plain object via the helper above. |

---

## 3. Full “before → after” example

### Before (Mapbox GL JS v2)

```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import 'mapbox-gl/dist/mapbox-gl.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.eyJ...';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12,
  pitch: 45,
  bearing: 0
});

map.on('load', () => {
  // Fog
  map.setFog({
    'color': '#f8f8f8',
    'high-color': '#ffffff',
    'horizon-blend': 0.3
  });

  // Free-camera: look from a high point down at a target
  const cam = map.getFreeCameraOptions();
  cam.center = [-122.42, 37.78];
  cam.altitude = 800;
  cam.pitch = 70;
  cam.bearing = 20;
  map.setFreeCameraOptions(cam);
});
```

### After (MapLibre GL JS v6)

```js
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

// No access token needed (unless your tile provider requires one)
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  // Use any style that serves its own tiles – e.g. OpenFreeMap or a self-hosted style.json
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12,
  pitch: 45,
  bearing: 0
});

map.on('load', () => {
  // SKY (replaces fog)
  map.setSky({
    'sky-color': '#f8f8f8',
    'horizon-color': '#ffffff',
    'fog-color': '#f8f8f8',
    'fog-ground-blend': 0.3,
    'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,
    'sky-horizon-blend': 0.3,
    'atmosphere-blend': 1.0
  });

  // Free-camera equivalent
  const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
    [-122.42, 37.78],   // lng/lat
    800,                // altitude (m)
    20,                 // bearing
    70,                 // pitch
    0                   // roll (optional)
  );

  // Choose the animation you prefer
  map.easeTo({ ...camOpts, duration: 1500 });
});
```

