## 6. What you **gain** and what you **lose** (quick recap)

| Gain | Lose |
|------|------|
| BSD-3-Clause open source, no vendor lock-in | Direct Mapbox Studio integration (styles must be exported & edited) |
| No mandatory access-token, free to self-host tiles | Mapbox-hosted vector tiles, sprites, glyphs, and the convenience of a single endpoint |
| Ability to use any vector-tile source (PMTiles, Martin, TileServer-GL, etc.) | Mapbox Search / Directions / Geocoding APIs (replace with open alternatives) |
| Community-driven roadmap, transparent releases | Official Mapbox support & SLA |
|

Below is a quick-reference guide that shows **all the practical ways you can add a geocoder / search box to a Mapbox GL JS v2 map**, together with the trade-offs you’ll face (license, cost, self-hosting, UI look-and-feel, API compatibility, etc.).  

I’ve split the options into three buckets:

| Bucket | What it is | When you’d pick it | How to add it (code snippets) | Key pros / cons |
|--------|------------|--------------------|------------------------------|-----------------|
| **A. Mapbox-official** | Mapbox-provided geocoder UI (Mapbox GL Geocoder) or the newer **Mapbox Search SDK** (UI + API) | You already have a Mapbox access token, need the most feature-complete, turn-key UI, and are fine with Mapbox’s pricing / rate limits. | See sections **A1** and **A2** below. | ✅ Tight integration, autocomplete, biasing, address-level results, built-in UI. <br>❌ Vendor lock-in, usage limits, paid beyond free tier, requires a Mapbox token. |
| **B. Open-source / self-hosted** | Community-maintained geocoder controls that work with any vector-tile source (Mapbox, MapLibre, OpenStreetMap, etc.) | You want to avoid Mapbox fees, need an open-source licence, or plan to self-host the search backend. | See sections **B1–B4**. | ✅ Free / self-hostable, no token needed, can be swapped for any map library. <br>❌ You must provision / choose a search service (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, etc.) and sometimes style the UI yourself. |
| **C. Custom UI + any API** | Build your own input box and call any geocoding endpoint (Mapbox, MapTiler, OpenCage, etc.) | You need a very specific UI, want to combine multiple providers, or want to keep the UI completely separate from the map library. | See section **C**. | ✅ Full control over UX, can mix providers. <br>❌ More code to write, you lose the ready-made “addControl” integration. |

---

## A. Mapbox-official Geocoder Options

### A1. **Mapbox GL Geocoder** (the classic plugin)

*Package*: `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`  
*Works with*: Mapbox GL JS v2 (and v1) – also works with MapLibre GL JS if you replace the token and style.  

**Installation**

```bash
npm i @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder
# or via CDN
# <script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>
# <link href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css" rel="stylesheet" />
```

**Basic usage**

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // required to use the built-in UI control
  placeholder: 'Search places',
  // optional: limit results to a country, bias to a viewport, etc.
  // countries: 'us,ca',
  // bbox: [-124.8, 24.5, -66.9, 49.5],
});

map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');   // or 'top-right', 'bottom-left', …
```

**Features you get out-of-the-box**

| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Autocomplete** | Shows suggestions as the user types. |
| **Result types** | Addresses, POIs, places, postcodes, etc. |
| **Proximity bias** | `proximity: [lng, lat]` automatically set to map center. |
| **Country / language filtering** | `countries`, `language` options. |
| **Fly-to on select** | The control automatically calls `map.flyTo()` to the result. |
| **Reverse geocode on click** | `geocoder.on('result', ...)` gives you the full feature. |
| **Custom UI** | You can embed the geocoder in any DOM node (`geocoder.addTo('#myDiv')`). |

**Limits & costs**

* Free tier: 100 000 forward geocoding requests / month (as of 2026).  
* Paid tier: $0.75 per 1 000 requests beyond the free tier.  
* Rate-limit: 600 req / min per token (soft limit; you’ll get a 429 if you exceed it).  

If you stay under the free tier, you can use it without any extra cost. Once you exceed it, you’ll need to add a payment method in the Mapbox dashboard.

---

### A2. **Mapbox Search SDK (UI + API)**

*Package*: `@mapbox/search-js` (UI) + `@mapbox/search-js-core` (API) – the newer “Search” platform that supersedes the classic Geocoder for many use-cases.  

**Why you might choose it**

* More modern UI (type-ahead, “search as you type” with better ranking).  
* Supports **search-as-you-type** for POIs, addresses, and even “search-by-category”.  
* Allows **offline / pre-fetch** of tiles for mobile apps (via the Search SDK’s caching).  

**Installation**

```bash
npm i @mapbox/search-js @mapbox/search-js-core
# CSS
import '@mapbox/search-js/dist/search.css';
```

**Minimal example**

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import { SearchBox } from '@mapbox/search-js';
import '@mapbox/search-js/dist/search.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const searchBox = new SearchBox({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  container: 'search-container',   // any existing DOM element
  // optional: limit to a country, set language, etc.
  // countries: ['us'],
  // language: 'en',
});

searchBox.on('result', (event) => {
  const { result } = event; // a GeoJSON Feature
  map.flyTo({ center: result.geometry.coordinates, zoom: 14 });
});
```

**Pricing**

The Search SDK uses the same **Mapbox Geocoding** pricing model (free tier + per-request cost). The UI component itself is free, but each request counts against your Geocoding quota.

---

## B. Open-source / Self-hosted Geocoder Controls

If you want to **avoid Mapbox fees** or you’re already planning to move to **MapLibre GL JS**, you’ll need a geocoder that does **not** depend on a Mapbox token. The good news is that the Mapbox GL Geocoder control has been **forked** and works with any map library that follows the same `addControl` contract.

| Option | Backend (search engine) | How to add it | Typical cost |
|--------|------------------------|---------------|--------------|
| **B1. maplibre-gl-geocoder** (fork of Mapbox GL Geocoder) | Any HTTP geocoding service (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler, OpenCage, etc.) | `npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder` | Free (backend may cost) |
| **B2. Leaflet Control Geocoder** (works with MapLibre via a tiny wrapper) | Same as B1 | `npm i leaflet-control-geocoder` + wrapper | Free |
| **B3. Algolia Places** (deprecated but still usable) | Algolia’s hosted index (free tier) | `npm i places.js` | Free up to 100 k req/mo |
| **B4. Custom UI + any API** | Any REST geocoder (Nominatim, OpenCage, MapTiler, etc.) | Write your own input + fetch | Depends on provider |

Below are the two most common “plug-and-play” solutions (B1 & B2) with code examples.

### B1. **@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder** (the community fork)

> **TL;DR** – Install the control, point it at a geocoding endpoint of your choice, and add it to the map exactly like the Mapbox version.

**Installation**

```bash
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder
# CSS
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';
```

**Using the public Nominatim demo (good for testing only)**

```javascript
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';

const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  // Nominatim public endpoint – **DO NOT** use in production!
  // For production, self-host Nominatim or use a managed service.
  url: 'https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search',
  // optional: add `params: { countrycodes: 'us', addressdetails: 1 }`
  placeholder: 'Search OSM places',
  // If you have a token for a paid service (e.g., MapTiler Geocoding), set `accessToken`.
});

map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');
```

**Switching to a production-grade backend**

| Backend | URL (example) | How to get a key (if needed) |
|--------|---------------|------------------------------|
| **Nominatim (self-hosted)** | `https://my-nominatim.org/search` | No key, but you must host it yourself (Docker image available). |
| **Photon (hosted by Komoot)** | `https://photon.komoot.io/api/` | No key, but rate-limited; self-host for production. |
| **Pelias (open-source)** | `https://my-pelias.org/v1/search` | No key; you run the service. |
| **MapTiler Geocoding** | `https://api.maptiler.com/geocoding/{query}.json` | Free tier 100 k req/mo, then $0.5/1 k. |
| **OpenCage** | `https://api.opencagedata.com/geocode/v1/json` | Free tier 2 500 req/day, then $50/1 M. |
| **OpenRouteService (geocode + routing)** | `https://api.openrouteservice.org/geocode/search` | Free tier 2 500 req/day, then paid plans. |

**Key differences from the Mapbox plugin**

| Feature | Mapbox GL Geocoder | MapLibre-GL Geocoder |
|---------|-------------------|----------------------|
| **Token handling** | `accessToken` required | No token required; you supply `url` (and optional `accessToken` for services that need it). |
| **CSS class prefix** | `.mapboxgl-...` | `.maplibregl-...` (the control automatically uses the new prefix). |
| **Supported map libraries** | Mapbox GL only (but works with MapLibre if you ignore the token) | Works with MapLibre GL, Mapbox GL (v1), and any library that implements the `IControl` interface. |
| **Bundling** | UMD & ESM | ESM only (v6+ of MapLibre). |

---

### B2
